    "body": "Ah just found this thread too – @trusktr you read my mind!\r\n\r\nI would love to be able to draw to WebGL/Canvas after layout and observer callbacks.\r\n\r\nThe sequencing I would love as an app-builder:\r\n1. requestAnimationFrame: do changes to DOM based on user inputs\r\n2. Layout calculates\r\n3. Observer callbacks from layout changes\r\n4. Draw to WebGL/Canvas based on new info from my observers\r\n\r\nWithout the proposed API, my draw calls are done in the rAF and are always one frame behind the DOM layout.\r\n\r\nI'd assume that DOM changes made in this callback would not process until the next frame (or could even error, etc)\r\n\r\nI am very likely missing some nuance here. I just wanted to help demonstrate why this sequencing is important in app-builder-land. I make design tools in the browser and often use a full screen canvas layered over top of DOM to draw selections and highlights.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"100%\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6fc3f413-66cf-4a5e-8723-f4229e556517\">\r\n\r\n",
