    "body": "I created a [loopBeforePaint](https://github.com/StephenHaney/loopBeforePaint) helper repo as a workaround solution.\r\n\r\nIt triggers a ResizeObserver callback on every frame so that the developer gets a callback that runs reliably after layout but before paint.\r\n\r\nSo far this is working well for me, but there are some considerations:\r\n- If you modify the DOM at all in the callback, it will of course cause another round of layout calcs\r\n- The ResizeObserver callback might not be the final RO callback that happens in that frame. If another RO callback modifies the DOM, the measurements from your callback will be outdated (the repo tries to mitigate this by not adding its RO until the page is idle)\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: Kaiido provided a better implementation below so I updated the code in the repo. \r\n_Original method, no longer used: It originally placed a div into the document, observed it with an RO, and used a rAF to resize it each frame._\r\n\r\n",
